Scion: room for the physical aperture's twig alignment (large memory, no monitor).

Modifications to Apple's xnu (xnu-12377.121.6) and new files for it, Apple Public
Source License 2.0 (APSL-2.0); see https://www.opensource.apple.com/apsl/. Original
files: Apple Inc. These changes: Scion contributors. Apply in order after buildfix.sh.

SCION_NATIVE_PAC builds only. Without it arm_vm_physmap_init() asserts on a kernel with
no kexts: Apple's VMs boot a kernel collection whose read-only part (outside the
aperture) is bigger than the alignment waste; the open kernel's is not.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
index 756af52..7b4e928 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -1885,6 +1885,9 @@ arm_vm_init(uint64_t memory_size, boot_args * args)
 	/* For large memory systems with no PPL such as virtual machines */
 	static_memory_end = phystokv(args->topOfKernelData);
 	physmap_end = physmap_base + real_phys_size;
+#if SCION_NATIVE_PAC
+	physmap_end += PTOV_TABLE_SIZE * ARM_TT_TWIG_SIZE;     /* worst-case twig alignment, as below */
+#endif
 #else
 	static_memory_end = physmap_base + mem_size + (PTOV_TABLE_SIZE * ARM_TT_TWIG_SIZE); // worst possible case for block alignment
 	physmap_end = physmap_base + real_phys_size + (PTOV_TABLE_SIZE * ARM_TT_TWIG_SIZE);
